    [ '2026-11-23', 'Commissions', 'Messages to a commission customer: write a “Note to customer” in the order’s Order notes box. On a commission order it goes out as a commission message from the commissions address (with a copy to you) instead of WooCommerce’s “A note has been added to your order”, links to the commission page, carries the Approve final artwork button while the finished artwork is waiting, and shows in the customer’s Conversation. The stage does not change. A line under the notes box says this on every commission order.' ],
    [ '2026-11-23', 'Commissions', 'Customer emails reach the Conversation again: the ten-minute check had stopped on Nov 17 and now runs again. It reads only Gmail (labels Commissions and Website Inquiries, and Sent Mail) since the info@, sales@ and commissions@ mailboxes became Gmail filters. Every email it adds is also filed in the commission’s records folder, so the off-line copy on the drive has the whole correspondence.' ],
    [ '2026-11-23', 'Commissions', 'The finished-artwork email now asks clearly for approval: its subject says “Action needed”, a boxed section explains that only the Approve final artwork button counts (not a reply or “Looks great”), and a large button opens the commission page right at that button. The customer’s commission page says the same at the top and leaves out “Approved so far” once the finished artwork is shared. The email no longer greets twice when your message starts with “Hi”.' ],
    [ '2026-11-23', 'Behind the scenes', 'Settings > monospace Kit lists the parts every monospace site shares, with a switch for each. Twelve of them started on this site (the lightbox, Hide this block, Remove background, Used in, AI descriptions, HEIC uploads and more); here they are marked “This site has its own”, and the other monospace sites now get them too.' ],
    [ '2026-11-23', 'Shop', 'Items bought for another monospace site now say where they come from: a Sightings print shows “From: Sightings” under its name in the cart, at checkout, on the order pages, in the order emails and on the admin order screen. The art site’s own pieces get no line. The cart also shares its item count with the other monospace sites, so the cart button on Sightings shows how many items are waiting.' ],
    [ '2026-11-23', 'Behind the scenes', 'One shared kit on every monospace site: the Contact page form and the cookie banner’s Google consent now come from the site’s own “monospace Kit” plugin, the same one the other monospace sites use. Contact Form 7 and Site Kit are gone, and six plugins that were already switched off (Stripe Tax, User Switching, WooCommerce Tax, the WooCommerce.com Update Manager and the CSV importer / exporter) were taken out.' ],
    [ '2026-11-23', 'Behind the scenes', 'Google consent mode now really starts as “denied” before any Google tag loads, so nothing from Google counts a visitor until they accept the cookie banner.' ],
    [ '2026-11-22', 'Behind the scenes', 'Error logs are kept lean: the site no longer writes debug chatter (stock syncs, cart discounts, bulk edits) to its logs, every error log on the hosting account is trimmed every night to the last 30 days (at most 1 MB each), and long background jobs can no longer run out of memory in the site’s cache. The 126 MB of old logs were archived and cleared.' ],
    [ '2026-11-22', 'Commissions', 'Sharing an update on a commission order is now reliable on a phone: photos are made smaller before they are sent, a progress bar shows how far the upload is, and if the connection stalls the screen finds out from the site whether the update went out and says so plainly (sent, still being sent, or not sent and safe to send again). The same update can never be emailed twice, and after a reload the box tells you what happened to your last update.' ],
    [ '2026-11-22', 'Prints', 'The postcard is now an option wherever prints are made or managed: New artwork, New prints, an artwork’s Prints box, All prints, the Artwork Editor (its own P chip, Show / Hide, Add / Remove, bulk actions) and the Quick Artwork Editor (summary, Postcard ID and its price card message). New artworks get a postcard along with their other prints, and a print added to an artwork whose prints are all hidden starts hidden too.' ],
    [ '2026-11-22', 'Prints', 'Every artwork with prints now also has a 4x6 postcard. Artworks whose prints are on sale show a Postcard tab on the price card; where all prints are hidden the postcard is hidden too, and Show prints / Hide prints treat it like the other prints. Tall pictures are sent to the printer turned sideways so they fill the card, while the shop keeps showing them upright.' ],
    [ '2026-11-22', 'Behind the scenes', 'Added a shared background job that makes a new print size for many artworks a few at a time, hidden until all are done. The Sightings postcards and these postcards now use the same job and the same turned-picture step.' ],
    [ '2026-11-21', 'Prints', 'Sightings drawings can now be bought as a 4x6 postcard. All 31 drawings in all three looks have one. The postcard is printed from a turned copy of the drawing so it fills the card, and it stays hidden in this shop for now.' ],
    [ '2026-11-21', 'Behind the scenes', 'Added a background job that makes one new print size for every Sightings drawing a few at a time, skips what exists and stops by itself. It was used to make all the postcards.' ],
